    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1088">

                <pb facs="0796" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4004.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul, Matamoros, telegraphs Department that it is impossible to assist
                    Americans at Saltillo. Department authorizes you to send such special messengers
                    as may be necessary in your judgment to extend protection to Americans in
                    Saltillo. Department regrets that it has no accurate information regarding
                    conditions at Saltillo and therefore must entrust to your accurate knowledge of
                    situation as it exists to-day the measure of relief which should be
                    extended.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
